        "title": "Precision Metrology",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Metrology is **the science of measurement** — establishing that a component's actual geometry, surface, and properties are within specified limits. No manufacturing process produces perfect parts; metrology determines whether the parts produced are acceptable. The central framework is **tolerance**: the allowable variation around a nominal dimension that still permits the part to function. Everything downstream — gauging, CMM, SPC — is a system for verifying conformance to tolerance."
    }
